Honour --codec=-sbc for the A2DP source, as FiiO's stock BlueALSA 4.0.0 on the Disc does.

Upstream forces SBC on ("mandatory codec"). Disco starts BlueALSA with only the chosen codec (LDAC, aptX, aptX HD)
so a connection is born on it; with SBC forced on, the stock player's route-time SBC request (06b3, value 0) switches
the headphones back to SBC under the music. SBC stays forced on when no other A2DP source codec is enabled, so the
daemon can never end up offering nothing.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -560,7 +560,13 @@
 #endif
 
 	/* Make sure that mandatory codecs are enabled. */
-	a2dp_sbc_source.enabled = true;
+	/* (diskOS Disco: SBC as a source only when no other source codec is on.) */
+	bool other_source = false;
+	for (struct a2dp_codec * const *cc = a2dp_codecs; *cc != NULL; cc++)
+		if ((*cc)->dir == A2DP_SOURCE && *cc != &a2dp_sbc_source && (*cc)->enabled)
+			other_source = true;
+	if (!other_source)
+		a2dp_sbc_source.enabled = true;
 	a2dp_sbc_sink.enabled = true;
 	config.hfp.codecs.cvsd = true;
 
